urname>Varmus</surname><given-names>HE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>A nucleoprotein complex mediates the integration of retroviral DNA</article-title><source>Genes Dev</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>469</fpage><lpage>478</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2721960</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030156-b019"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fassati</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Goff</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Characterization of intracellular reverse transcription complexes of Moloney murine leukemia virus</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>73</volume><fpage>8919</fpage><lpage>8925</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10515996</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030156-b020"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Olvera</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Yoder</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitchell</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Butler</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Role of the non-homologous DNA end joining pathway in the early steps of retroviral infection</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>3272</fpage><lpage>3281</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11406603</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030156-b021"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yamashita</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Emerman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Capsid is a dominant determinant of retrovirus infectivity in nondividing cells</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>78</volume><fpage>5670</fpage><lpage>5678</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15140964</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030156-b022"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>von Schwedler</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Kornbluth</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Trono</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>The nuclear localization signal of the matrix protein of human immunodeficiency virus type 1 allows the establishment of infection in macrophages and quiescent T lymphocytes</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>91</volume><fpage>6992</fpage><lpage>6996</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8041734</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030156-b023"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sladek</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobberger</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Cell cycle analysis of retroviral vector gene expression during early infection</article-title><source>Cytometry</source><volume>31</volume><fpage>235</fpage><lpage>241</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9551598</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030156-b024"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Alin</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Goff</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Amino acid substitutions in the CA protein of Moloney murine leukemia virus that block early events in infection</article-title><source>Virology</source><volume>222</volume><fpage>339</fpage><lpage>351</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8806518</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030156-b025"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="